    "body": "### Problem\n\n`vim.treesitter.select()` does not respect the option `selection=exclusive`\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim --clean test.lua`\n2. `:set selection=exclusive`\n3. input some code:\n```lua\nfunction()\n\tprint(\"hello\")\nend\n```\n4. put the cursor inside `hello`\n5. type `van`, the default keymap\n6. the select range is `hell`, not the `hello`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nshould respect the option `selection=exclusive`\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1183+g7b28b1f4a9\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\n6.18.26.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nWindows terminal\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\ngithub packages",
